`dataSource.find()` is defined to return a `QueryResult` (with a `data` array), but this extraction only checks `records` on object responses. With the current ObjectStackAdapter returning `{ data, total, ... }`, `data` will always stay empty here and charts won’t render. Update the normalization to also handle `results.data` (and keep `records` as a secondary fallback if needed).
```suggestion
                const obj = results as any;
                if (Array.isArray(obj.data)) {
                    data = obj.data;
                } else if (Array.isArray(obj.records)) {
                    data = obj.records;
```
